---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';

import keyArt from '@media/nova-trailer-banner.jpg';
import trailerUrl from '@media/nova-trailer-preview.mp4';

// The poster is what a visitor looks at until they press play, so it earns the
// same optimisation pass as any other image on the page.
const poster = await getImage({ src: keyArt, width: 1600, format: 'webp' });
---

<section class="border-t border-hairline bg-abyss py-20 sm:py-28" aria-labelledby="trailer-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[72rem] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[46rem]" data-reveal>
      <p class="label">The trailer</p>
      <h2 id="trailer-heading" class="display-sm mt-4 text-[clamp(1.75rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)] text-ink">
        The hauler that never checked for acid
      </h2>
      <p class="prose-copy mt-4">
        Two runs, eighty-one seconds. First light: one android, one charger, and a board nobody has looked at yet. Then
        a colony program that has grown into an industry — extractors working the ground, a corridor of depots, a colony
        module going up while the readiness score climbs. And a hauler on version three of a script whose routing never
        learned to read <code class="font-mono text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-dim">composition.acid</code>, walking east
        across the flats. Its last broadcast outlives it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 90ms">
      {
        /*
        `preload="none"` on purpose: the file is 4MB, and a visitor who does not
        press play should never pay for it. The poster carries the frame instead.
      */
      }
      <video
        class="w-full rounded-[0.625rem] border border-hairline bg-void"
        controls
        playsinline
        preload="none"
        poster={poster.src}
        width="1600"
        height="900"
      >
        <source src={trailerUrl} type="video/mp4" />
        Your browser cannot play this video.
        <a class="text-system underline" href={trailerUrl}>Download the trailer instead.</a>
      </video>
      {
        /* The provenance note sits under the video rather than above it. It is
          worth saying — a trailer that is really the game is unusual enough to
          claim — but not at the cost of a visitor learning how the film was made
          before they learn what it is of. */
      }
      <figcaption class="mt-3 max-w-[52rem] text-[0.875rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        81 seconds, with sound. Not a mock-up: both acts are ordinary Nova recordings — the same JSON files
        <code class="font-mono text-[0.8125rem]">nova play</code> opens — replayed through the game's own renderer one frame
        at a time. The script in the code panel is the script stored in the recording, and the readiness numbers come from
        the same scoring function <code class="font-mono text-[0.8125rem]">nova status</code> uses.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
